# Prompt history (`PROMPTS.md`)

After you complete **user-driven** work that changes behavior, features, data model, or notable UX (not tiny typo-only edits unless the user asks), **append a new entry to `PROMPTS.md`** so the team can share context later.

## How to append

- Add **below the latest entry** (file header says newest at bottom).
- Use this shape (match existing entries):

```markdown
---

## YYYY-MM-DD (n)

**Prompt:**

> (verbatim or faithful paraphrase of what the user asked)

**Outcome:** Short summary: files touched, main decision, 1–2 lines max.
```

- Number `(n)` only if there are multiple entries the same calendar day (continue the sequence in the file).
- One entry per coherent task; you may merge closely related messages from the same session into a single entry.

## Do not log

- Pure refactors with no user request, internal tooling, or negligible one-line fixes—unless the user explicitly wants it recorded.

## Related docs

